{"id": "EUVD-2026-93151", "enisaUuid": "89c279c6-1818-3993-b74e-18928b3b685d", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmm: filemap: retain mapped dropbehind folios\n\nFault-around can map ready dropbehind folios without going through the\nnormal page-cache lookup that clears dropbehind.  A mapping represents a\ncompeting cached user, so retain the folio instead of forcibly unmapping\nit when writeback completes.\n\nFor a mapped folio, folio_unmap_invalidate() can call\nunmap_mapping_folio(), which takes i_mmap_rwsem and may sleep.  Retaining\nmapped folios avoids this path when folio_end_dropbehind() runs in\nnon-preemptible task context.\n\nTal was able to trigger a sleeping-in-atomic warning due to this [1].\n\nUnmapped dropbehind folios continue through the existing invalidation path.", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:44:58", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:15:55", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2897601dffe576fcd87a4259102f41f7fb0cbfc8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/77c0fade37c80e8aa16ac048a9828249055e3f66", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/848d2ce2fce15fbdc083fbf9691bfa72911033c4"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98223", "GHSA-h9mh-jjx8-7v74"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "3c47e002-31f3-3986-a4e2-617a4d2c7880", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "4465f3a4-2bf3-35e2-a624-f5ce60562a84", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.8"}, {"id": "70e40ee7-e733-3ba2-93c0-a65e7bb88973", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.14"}, {"id": "bf69bcf4-fef5-3828-a34f-c2f0b4e7f644", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "fb7d3bc4149395c1ae99029c852eab6c28fc3c88 <77c0fade37c80e8aa16ac048a9828249055e3f66"}, {"id": "ded42b7a-c4a1-36a5-a632-74d2b707fda1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.54"}, {"id": "e336ea19-201c-3f72-a7c4-bf009e707e31", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "fb7d3bc4149395c1ae99029c852eab6c28fc3c88 <2897601dffe576fcd87a4259102f41f7fb0cbfc8"}, {"id": "ed604043-18af-3cc3-a23a-117422fe96f8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "fb7d3bc4149395c1ae99029c852eab6c28fc3c88 <848d2ce2fce15fbdc083fbf9691bfa72911033c4"}, {"id": "ff2c322f-d0ea-3bbb-98a6-e59466d50906", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "1b6cc426-b84f-39de-bb2c-3df859eaf90c", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}